to a content archive Make a Selection Document Center\n- News & Notices\n- Useful Links\n- Forms & Applications Frequently Asked Questions\nHome\nGovernment\nRecorder\nRecorder\nThe elective office of county recorder was the first local office created by the Constitution of the state of Indiana in 1816. It is the primary duty of county recorders to record instruments submitted for recording and maintaining those records for perpetuity. These instruments include deeds, mortgages, surveys, liens, releases, powers of attorney, military discharges, assumed business name, UCC’s, and many other documents.\nVisit the Recorder's FAQ Section to understand how to transfer or modify a name on property and to get copies of deeds.\nNEWS\nLINKS\nFORMS\nNews\nDoxpop Property Watch\nAttorney General Todd Rokita warns Hoosiers of government imposter scams Attorney General Todd Rokita is warning Hoosiers to be alert to government imposter scams, which continue to ...\nRecorder's Fee Schedule\nList of fees for the Recorder's Office.\nNews Release introducing new process for tracking veteran discharge records\nIndiana Department of Veterans Affairs introduce new process for tracking veteran discharge records.\nUseful Links\nDoxpop Property Watch\nForms\nCertificate of Assumed Business Name Form\nFOUNTAIN COUNTY, IN\n301 4th St., Covington, IN 47932 • M-F 8:00am - 4:00pm • 765-793-5000 • Staff Directory\n© 2026 Fountain County, Indiana\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility Statement\nTerms of Use\n-->\nSite Design and Content Management by\nCORE Business Technologies",
